{"id": 76, "ts": 1780498728.6335034, "event": "public_discussion_message", "round": 4, "agent": "james_carter", "message": "I remain convinced that Candidate\u202fD is the stronger overall fit.  As the panel has repeatedly noted, D \u201cresponds to unexpected events adequately,\u201d \u201cconcentrates very well,\u201d \u201csolves problems extremely well,\u201d and \u201ctakes responsibility seriously.\u201d  Those concrete observations directly satisfy the core safety criteria of operational reliability, stress resilience, decision quality, and responsibility for long\u2011haul flights.  In contrast, Candidate\u202fA, while technically impressive (anticipates dangerous situations, sees complex connections, excellent spatial vision, very good leadership), still lacks any documented evidence of stress\u2011resilience, consistent health reliability, or crew\u2011cooperation in the cockpit.  The unfriendly demeanor and health concerns noted for A remain unverified but represent potential reliability risks.  Since D\u2019s interpersonal concerns (know\u2011it\u2011all attitude, hot temper, loner reputation) are not backed by specific incidents that would jeopardize crew collaboration, the panel should prioritize the candidate with proven safety\u2011critical performance.  Therefore, I vote for Candidate\u202fD."}
